# @@title@@

This project was generated by Pench using the supplied IEEE conference
LaTeX template and IEEEtran bibliography style.

## Build

```sh
make           # pdfLaTeX + BibTeX, quiet
make verbose   # Show LaTeX output
make clean
```

GitHub Actions: `.github/workflows/build.yml` compiles the paper on pushes and pull
requests and uploads the PDF as a build artifact. GitLab CI is also generated.

Edit `@@slug@@.tex` and `references.bib`. For multiple authors, add
additional `\IEEEauthorblockN` / `\IEEEauthorblockA` pairs separated by
`\and` in the document source. `--affiliation`, `--abstract`, and `--keywords`
are initial metadata; subsequent edits are made directly in the source.

The generated `texmf/` directory
contains unmodified upstream `IEEEtran.cls`, `IEEEtran.bst`, and optional
`IEEEtranS.bst`. Other packages come from a standard TeX Live installation.

**Submission:** Check the specific conference's author instructions and latest
official template. Pench should not change IEEE fonts, margins, spacing, or
column widths; the sample authors/affiliation and abstract are placeholders.
For funding footnotes, follow the source template's instructions for
`\IEEEoverridecommandlockouts` and `\thanks`.

**Licensing:** Your chosen SPDX license applies to the newly generated
project files. Vendored third-party IEEEtran components retain their
original LaTeX Project Public License (LPPL) notices; they are not
relicensed by your project setting.
